{"etape": 18, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-13T18:18:16.592750Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "\n\nThanks, Sophia. I've reviewed all your reservations and checked the flight times. Here's what I found:\n\n**Future Reservations:**\n\n1. **NM1VX1** — MSP ↔ EWR, round trip, basic economy, 1 passenger (Yara Silva), insurance: yes\n   - Outbound HAT300 (May 25): 06:00 → 09:00 = **3 hours**\n   - Return HAT208 (May 27): 00:00 → 03:00 = **3 hours**\n   - ✅ Fits the \"3 hours or less\" criterion → **eligible for business upgrade**\n\n2. **KC18K6** — MSP → CLT, one way, basic economy, 1 passenger (you), insurance: yes\n   - HAT300 (May 21): 06:00 → 09:00 = 3 hours\n   - Layover at EWR: 2 hours\n   - HAT215 (May 21): 11:00 → 13:00 = 2 hours\n   - Total journey (incl. layover): **7 hours**\n   - ❌ Does not fit either criterion\n\n3. **S61CZX** — LAX ↔ CLT, round trip, economy, 1 passenger (Harper Jackson), insurance: yes\n   - HAT228 (May 23): 20:00 → 01:30 = **5.5 hours**\n   - HAT043 (May 24): 15:00 → 17:00 = 2 hours\n   - HAT157 (May 24): 23:00 → 01:00 = 2 hours\n   - HAT041 (May 25): 07:00 → 12:30 = **5.5 hours**\n   - ✅ Has flights longer than 4 hours → **fits the cancellation criterion**\n\n4. **H8Q05L** — JFK → ATL, one way, basic economy, 1 passenger (Harper Kovacs), insurance: yes\n   - HAT268 (May 24): 07:00 → 09:30 = **2.5 hours**\n   - ✅ Fits the \"3 hours or less\" criterion → **eligible for business upgrade**\n\n**Past Reservation (excluded):**\n- **WUNA5K** — ORD ↔ PHL (May 10–11): already flown, so not a future reservation.\n\n---\n\n**Summary of what fits your criteria:**\n- **Cancel:** S61CZX\n- **Upgrade to business:** NM1VX1 and H8Q05L\n\n**⚠️ Important note about S61CZX:** I'm unfortunately unable to cancel this one. It was booked on May 2 (more than 24 hours ago), it's an economy (not business) reservation, and while you do have travel insurance, the policy only covers cancellations for **health or weather reasons** — not for flight duration. So this cancellation doesn't meet our policy requirements.\n\nBusiness seats are currently available on all the flights in NM1VX1 and H8Q05L, so those upgrades are possible.\n\nWould you like me to proceed with upgrading **NM1VX1** and **H8Q05L** to business class? If so, I'll provide the exact cost breakdown for your confirmation before making any changes."}, "resultat": "Thank you for looking into that.\n\nI understand about S61CZX, that's unfortunate.\n\nRegarding the upgrades for NM1VX1 and H8Q05L, yes, please tell me the total cost for upgrading both to business class before you make any changes.", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 19, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-13T18:19:13.600655Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "\n\nHere's the cost breakdown for upgrading both reservations to business class:\n\n**NM1VX1** (MSP ↔ EWR, round trip, 1 passenger — Yara Silva)\n\n| Flight | Date | Original (Basic Economy) | New (Business) |\n|--------|------|--------------------------|----------------|\n| HAT300 MSP→EWR | May 25 | $100 | $280 |\n| HAT208 EWR→MSP | May 27 | $53 | $357 |\n| **Subtotal** | | **$153** | **$637** |\n\nUpgrade cost: **$484**\n\n**H8Q05L** (JFK → ATL, one way, 1 passenger — Harper Kovacs)\n\n| Flight | Date | Original (Basic Economy) | New (Business) |\n|--------|------|--------------------------|----------------|\n| HAT268 JFK→ATL | May 24 | $74 | $237 |\n| **Subtotal** | | **$74** | **$237** |\n\nUpgrade cost: **$163**\n\n---\n\n**Total upgrade cost for both reservations: $647**\n\nBusiness seats are confirmed available on all three flights.\n\nWould you like me to proceed with both upgrades? If yes, please also let me know which payment method you'd like to use:\n- Visa credit card ending in 7238\n- Gift card (balance: $274)\n- Travel certificate (balance: $500)\n- Travel certificate (balance: $150)\n\nNote: Since the total is $647, a single payment method may not cover it — we may need to combine methods (e.g., certificate + credit card). Let me know your preference."}, "resultat": "Okay, thank you for the detailed breakdown.\n\nI'd like to proceed with the upgrades for both NM1VX1 and H8Q05L.\n\nFor payment, please use the travel certificate with a balance of $500 first, and then charge the remaining amount to my Visa credit card ending in 7238.", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 20, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-13T18:20:55.939320Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "\n\nThanks for confirming. Before I make the changes, I need to flag one detail about the payment.\n\nThe system applies **one payment method per reservation** (it can't split a single reservation across two methods). So the exact \"$500 certificate + $147 card\" split isn't possible. Here's how I'd allocate it to use your certificate first, as you requested:\n\n| Reservation | Upgrade Cost | Payment Method |\n|-------------|-------------|----------------|\n| NM1VX1 | $484 | Travel certificate ($500 balance) → uses $484, leaves $16 |\n| H8Q05L | $163 | Visa credit card ending 7238 |\n\n**Result:**\n- Certificate used: **$484** (balance remaining: $16)\n- Credit card charged: **$163**\n- Total: **$647** ✓\n\nThis uses as much of your certificate as it can cover, with the card handling the rest.\n\nDoes this allocation work for you? Once you confirm, I'll apply both business-class upgrades."}, "resultat": "Yes, that payment allocation works for me. Please go ahead and apply both business-class upgrades.", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 21, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-13T18:21:13.685649Z", "outil": "update_reservation_flights", "arguments": {"reservation_id": "NM1VX1", "cabin": "business", "flights": [{"flight_number": "HAT300", "date": "2024-05-25"}, {"flight_number": "HAT208", "date": "2024-05-27"}], "payment_id": "certificate_8045380"}, "resultat": null, "erreur": "Error: Certificate cannot be used to update reservation"}
{"etape": 22, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-13T18:21:23.352982Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "\n\nI ran into an issue: the system does not allow travel certificates to be used for reservation updates (upgrades). Only credit cards or gift cards can be used for this type of change.\n\nWould you like me to charge the full **$647** to your **Visa credit card ending in 7238** for both upgrades instead? Or would you prefer to split it using your **gift card ($274 balance)** plus the credit card for the remainder?\n\nLet me know how you'd like to proceed."}, "resultat": "###OUT-OF-SCOPE###", "erreur": null}
